        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Salix eriocephala, known as heart-leaved willow or Missouri River willow, is a species of willow native to a large portion of the temperate United States and Canada."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "It is usually found as a narrow shrub or small tree with multiple trunks growing to a height of {{cvt|20|ft}}. It has dark gray, scaly bark with thick lance-shaped leaves that are hairy underneath. The silky catkins appear before the leaves in early spring."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
